% Origin: Kowalski, *Computational Logic and Human Thinking*,
%         Chapter 6 "How to Become a British Citizen", section 6.2,
%         Example 4 ("Informal CL representation of subsection 1.1" of the
%         British Nationality Act 1981).
% Last verification: no open issues (no errors/warnings; all tests pass).
%
% Book rule (informal CL): X acquires british citizenship by subsection 1.1
% at time T if X is a person and X is born in the uk at time T and T is after
% commencement and Y is a parent of X and (Y is a british citizen at time T or
% Y is settled in the uk at time T).
%
% We introduce the "parent" abstraction (parent = mother or father), as the
% book does, and split the disjunction in the body into two clauses (one for
% the british-citizen path, one for the settled-in-the-uk path). Dates use the
% same `*a date* is after commencement` scenario idiom as citizenship.le.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
*a person* acquires British citizenship by subsection 1.1 on *a date*.
*a person* is a parent of *a second person*.
*a person* is born in the UK on *a date*.
*a date* is after commencement.
*a person* is the mother of *a second person*.
*a person* is the father of *a second person*.
*a person* is a British citizen on *a date*.
*a person* is settled in the UK on *a date*.

the knowledge base bna citizenship includes:

% The parent abstraction: a parent is a mother or a father.
a person is a parent of a second person
    if the person is the mother of the second person.

a person is a parent of a second person
    if the person is the father of the second person.

% Subsection 1.1, british-citizen-parent path.
a person acquires British citizenship by subsection 1.1 on a date
    if the person is born in the UK on the date
    and the date is after commencement
    and a second person is a parent of the person
    and the second person is a British citizen on the date.

% Subsection 1.1, settled-in-the-uk-parent path.
a person acquires British citizenship by subsection 1.1 on a date
    if the person is born in the UK on the date
    and the date is after commencement
    and a second person is a parent of the person
    and the second person is settled in the UK on the date.

scenario mother_citizen is:
    John is born in the UK on 2021-10-09.
    2021-10-09 is after commencement.
    Alice is the mother of John.
    Alice is a British citizen on 2021-10-09.
    acquisition expects answers ["John acquires British citizenship by subsection 1.1 on 2021-10-9T0:0:0.0"].

scenario father_settled is:
    Mary is born in the UK on 2021-10-09.
    2021-10-09 is after commencement.
    Harry is the father of Mary.
    Harry is settled in the UK on 2021-10-09.
    acquisition expects answers ["Mary acquires British citizenship by subsection 1.1 on 2021-10-9T0:0:0.0"].

scenario father_citizen is:
    Tom is born in the UK on 2021-10-09.
    2021-10-09 is after commencement.
    George is the father of Tom.
    George is a British citizen on 2021-10-09.
    acquisition expects answers ["Tom acquires British citizenship by subsection 1.1 on 2021-10-9T0:0:0.0"].

query acquisition is:
    which person acquires British citizenship by subsection 1.1 on which date.
